For $\nu\vdash a$ and $b\ge0$, $$\label{tools:pieri}
 \mathop{\mathrm{Ind}}_{S_a\times S_b}^{S_{a+b}}
      (S^\nu\boxtimes\mathbf1)
 \cong
 \bigoplus_{\substack{\lambda\vdash a+b,\ \lambda\supseteq\nu\\
                      \lambda/\nu\text{ a horizontal strip}}}
       S^\lambda.$$ Every summand occurs once.

Let $\theta=(\theta_1,\ldots,\theta_\ell)\vdash n$. The row-tabloid permutation module has the equivalent induced realization $$M^\theta=
 \mathop{\mathrm{Ind}}_{S_{\theta_1}\times\cdots\times S_{\theta_\ell}}^{S_n}
 \mathbf1.$$ Then $S^\tau$ occurs in $M^\theta$ if and only if $\tau\unrhd\theta$, and $S^\theta$ occurs once. The word module of any content obtained by reordering the parts of $\theta$ is also isomorphic to $M^\theta$.

Let a finite group $G$ act transitively on a finite set $\Omega$. Suppose a $G$-module has a direct-sum decomposition $T=\bigoplus_{A\in\Omega}T_A$ with $gT_A=T_{gA}$. Fix $D\in\Omega$, let $H$ be its stabilizer, and take $z\in T_D$. If $A_0=\mathbb C[H]z$, then the map $$\label{band:induced-map}
 \Phi:\mathbb C[G]\otimes_{\mathbb C[H]}A_0\longrightarrow\mathbb C[G]z,
 \qquad g\otimes a\longmapsto ga$$ is an isomorphism of $G$-modules.

For the parameters in [band:sets](#band:sets), there is a surjective $G_m$-equivariant map $$\label{band:quotient}
 W_m\twoheadrightarrow
 \mathop{\mathrm{Ind}}_{S_D\times S_F}^{S_{B_m}}(W_h\boxtimes U_{m,s}).$$ In particular, every irreducible constituent of the induced module on the right is a constituent of $W_m$.

Let $e$ be the number of even positions among $p,\ldots,p+r-1$, and put $\delta=1$ if $p$ is even and $\delta=0$ otherwise. Then $$\label{path:segment-formula}
 A_{r,p}=r!(-1)^{e-\delta}M_1\cdots M_r.$$ In particular, all these matrices are invertible. Their values are $$\label{path:segment-table}
 \begin{array}{c|cc}
 r & p\text{ odd} & p\text{ even}\\ \hline
 1&I&I\\
 2&-2Z&2Z\\
 3&-6J&-6J\\
 4&-24I&24I
 \end{array}$$
